Who is Sukha?
How to reach
INDIA
When you arrive on Jamnikund road, just head straight for a few hundred meters until you see a signboard of SUKHA'S PLACE, there you turn right and after 20 meters on a little lane you have arrived!
Sukha is Sukha. His is just himself, like nobody else. Sukha is a person who loves life, always positive, always trying to make the best of every situation.
Sukha has been running various restaurants and hotels in Pushkar for more than fifteen years, and wherever he is, the place is filled with people, old friends and new friends. Anybody who stays in Sukha's Place becomes a friend.
Building his own SUKHA'S PLACE was his dream and in 2005 it came true, that's why he also calls his place SEPNA VILLAGE - 'sepna' in Hindi means dream.
He loves to learn and he travels a lot, but when he is away, you can still feel his spirit in his place.
"A wonderful place where I found peace, relax and my own space.. a good place to hide from the rush. It has a very helpful and interesting staff, a beautiful sand garden and a fire place where we used to sit and play some music and have nice talking.
The food is really good and tasty!! I enjoyed this place a lot!"
"SUKHA’S PLACE is a calm place just 15 minutes walk away from Pushkar, away from the sounds of cars and roads! I really liked the sandy open spaces and the alley of small flowering bushes. The place is ideal for who love to have an exchange with other travelers, here they come from all over the world, and we sat all together at a long table for dinner in the evening."
"It’s good life at SUKHA’S PLACE, it’s tranquil, it has space, it’s beautiful.. as well as the persons here who make the place alive.
The birds all around are wonderful ... It’s a perfect place for making meditation and yoga. Everything is simply great."
"The bungalows are clean, private and comfortable, they make a peaceful retreat for the evenings and with the sun streaming in, in the mornings, it is the perfect atmosphere to begin your day in."
The small holy pilgrimage town of Pushkar is situated in the centre of the magic desert state of Rajasthan in western India. Around the holy lake there are many temples, small sleepy lanes and a vivid bazaar with shops for any need and taste.
The town is enjoyed by many travellers for its quiet ambiance, beauty and opportunities for friendship with the local people.
SUKHA'S PLACE is a relaxing place in the outskirts of Pushkar, near enough to reach the market easily but far enough to enjoy tranquility.
Just at the feet of the beautiful Nagpahar mountains, surrounded by farmer's fields with flowers and vegetables, this is the place for you if you look for a laid back time while in Pushkar. A place to chill out with friends, sit by a fireplace in the evenings and eat great food.
