Our Vice President Vincent Feix returned to France in July to take on new missions at company headquarters after five years at your side.
He has been replaced by Mr Bert Vanmiddelem who we were happy to welcome amongst us at the beginning of April.
He will be working from Toronto and you can contact him at +1 (905) 699-2489.
Our phone number has also changed: Office/Fax: +1 450 844 6199.
Michel Tadjer, our DE LA BALLINA Inc. technical and service manager is based on these premises and remains at your disposal to meet all your requests (training, interventions, troubleshooting, spare part sales, etc.).
We will carry on developing this proximity and flexibility to better serve you.
A new name for De La Ballina
On 20th June, Société Générale launched its new web site http://www.histoires-dequipes.fr/ as part of its specific business oriented communication.
A campaign in the regional press accompanies the launch of this site which will tell the story of 13 French SMEs. It contains stories, video reports and photo reports of the directors and their employees.
These stories are true human adventures showing the strength of teamwork at the service of a company.
Each story tells the tale of a team of employees contributing to the success of their company.
De La Ballina is amongst the SMEs which were capable of adapting to their environment and has become one of the references in its sector of activity.
Europastry, founded 22 years ago by the visionary baker Don Pere Gallès, is now Spain's leading producer of deep frozen bakery products and pastries, with a market share of more than 35%. In recent years, it has also become one of the leading European players in the sector, thanks to the quality of its products and the permanent innovation of its Technical and R&D department, managed by Jordi Caballero.
In order to produce range-topping products that demand an optimal process, the group's Technical Director, Xavi Alonso, selected expert suppliers capable of delivering quality products and maximum system efficiency, while remaining sufficiently available to deliver made-to-measure service.
De La Ballina Industrie already supplies Europastry with automatic packaging solutions for 10 years.
DLB: What is the most important thing about your cooperation with DLB?
Jordi Caballero and Xavi Alonso: DLB has been part of our growth for 10 years now, delivering systems to almost every one of the group's sites. De La Ballina Industrie provides efficient counting, quality control and automatic product packaging solutions.
What are your thoughts on your collaboration on the latest production line at Vallmoll, dedicated to the famous Gran Reserva?
DLB has introduced a lot of innovations in the last three years (counting and quality control by 3D vision, increased throughput and efficiency of the lines, robotised box packing), which is why we decided to work with DLB on line N°7, in view of the diversity of the products and the flexibility of the solutions that they demand.
To package our top-of-the-range Gran Reserva products, we opted for a mixed solution that is capable of boxing ovalado or chapata type products with robots, while using a hopper-based system for other products, such as baguettes, half-baguettes and small products.
And what about the collaboration between DLB and Pattyn Packing Lines on this project?
We are quite satisfied with this collaboration.
DLB is an expert in product flows, while Pattyn Packing Lines is specialised in the control of bags and boxes. We already used Pattyn machines on certain sites. As far as line N°7 is concerned, each change raised doubts and questions amongst the operators.
The DS-11 bag sealer is also a good and reliable machine, without being a bottleneck in the line.
From artificial 3D vision to robotics,each modules are tested and adapted to your product and performancerequirements by our teams are optimally integrated into your production lines in order to guarantee the efficiency of your packaging lines.
Associated with a compact, reliable and flexible mechanical design, our different modules adapt to all of your production:
