It works using shape recognition or 3D techniques, according to your products.
The camera position above the machine identifies and defines the position of every product on the conveyor belt.
The data sent by the camera is used:
to count the products,
to determine their position in order to separate them into batches of pre-defined quantities.
This comb only allows the right number of products through and immediately stops the other products.
The PATTYN BAKERY DIVISION counting machine was designed to obey the following rules:
product batches must never contain count under specification,
the settings of the vision PLC are adjusted with an user friendly, color touch-sensitive screen. No special computer training is necessary.
the standard version of the counting machine can store up to 1,000 product sheets,
all your productiondata can be centralized on a PC.
After taking the first step in 2009, when De La Ballina started to operate as an independent business unit within the Pattyn Group, we are now going one step further.
De la Ballina has now become a fully integrated part of Pattyn, sharing the same identity, vision and values.
In the continuity of this integration the graphic identity of the Pattyn Group will be harmonized.
We are proud to announce that the new company name for "De La Ballina" will be "Pattyn Bakery Division" as from September 12, 2015, the start of the IBA show.
With this integration we create a long-term destination for our Bakery Division and a long-term relationship with you, our valued customer. Sharing the same values as integrity, passion, commitment, flexibility, and humour we remain your reliable partner in heart and mind.
Sharing a long tradition of innovation & technology and 50 years of experience we continue meeting your challenges. We are convinced that by combining our experience and know-how this will lead to smarter high-performance packaging solutions.
On a short term you will benefit from one service team, reachable at service@pattyn.com.
The "Pattyn Bakery Division" office and production site remains in Maleville. To be as close as possible to you, Pattyn Bakery Division will also stay present in Canada, Spain, Germany and Malaysia. Your personal contact remains at your service for all your pending and future bread packaging challenges.
Contact details are not changed, except for the personal and general e-mail addresses, which are standardized to simplify communication.
In the near future there will be one joint website: www.pattyn.com
