The metal detection module designed and manufactured by PATTYN BAKERY DIVISION is highly sensitive and very reliable.
It is designed to eject any products contaminated by retraction of the belt.
It is compact, robust and flexible.
Thanks to its independent frame, the metal detecting conveyor can be adapted to the leading manufacturer of detection heads available on the market.
Thanks to its 20 years of experience in industrial bakery, PATTYN BAKERY DIVISION chose to privilege:
ease of maintenance by limiting the number of parts used
quick channel change thanks to a tool-free fixture system
the lowest possible operational noise thanks to a vibration solution that is built into the channel
Available with 4, 6 or 8 channels, this machine is a cost effective solution when production is entirely dedicated to small products.
Associated with a bagger, it makes it possible to make up to 50 bags/minute or up to 15 cases when combined with a direct case packing solution.
Thanks to its upstream vision-based quality control, which is also used to drive scara 4 axis robots, only compliant products are packed after having been oriented.
Using a 7th mechanical axis and an additional 6 axis poly-articulated robot, the stacks of products are boxed.
