Airport information, and directions to get to Maracay.
How to get from Maracay to Choroní:
With private transportation:
After this point, the road descents, passing several small villages, until you will reach the village of Choroní. Passing through the village of Choroní you will get to Puerto Colombia. Entering Puerto Colombia, you will pass the new busterminal. After the terminal take the first to the left, entering a sandy road (on the corner posada Pittier).
Then you’ll take the first road to the right (on the corner posada Del Sol).
By bus, from Maracay:
From the bus-terminal in Maracay (“Terminal del Occidente”) you can take a bus directly to Choroní. These busses go as far as the bus-terminal of Puerto Colombia. You will have to walk further down the road.
After the terminal take the first to the left, entering a sandy road (on the corner posada Pittier).
If you are already in the centre of Puerto Colombia:
You will have to walk back until you reach the Guardia Nacional, and just before the Guardia Nacional, make a right turn entering a sandy road. Then turn left at the first road.
After that, take the second road to the right, where at the end you’ll see the sign of posada El Ancla. At El Ancla, take a left turn, and after about 30 meters, on your right hand side, you’ll find our main entrance.
