Choroní is known for its beautiful beaches, but also for its nightlife!
The Malecón of Puerto Colombia is an ideal place to walk a while, sit down in the evening, meet other people, browse or purchase local art or eat a hot-dog or hamburger.
During weekends (mainly on Saturday nights), this is the spot where the “Tambores de Choroní” (traditional drums) play their music, while the spectators are encouraged to join in to sing and dance with them.
Here are some sites we can recommend to have a beer or something stronger:
A world under water:
Get to know a completely different world: The underwater world.
Around Choroní you can find various different locations in which you can see the world of coral and fish from up-close.
With only a diving mask and snorkel, or with a complete diving outfit, you’ll always see something beautiful.
With a diving mask and snorkel you can very well observe the underwater world in the natural pool of “Valle Seco”. Valle Seco is a beach which you can reach by boat from Puerto Colombia in about 15 minutes. It is also suitable for beginners.
The natural pool is formed by a coral reef, at about 15 meters from the beach.
Other good locations for snorkeling are: Cepe (only if there are few waves) and La Ciénaga.
For those who like some more than snorkeling, there’s the possibility to explore the underwater world using dive equipment.
If you have got a diving licence, you can rent equipment and/or make guided dives.
When possible André, Cachama Negra’s owner, will join you to make underwater pictures.
Photo gallery: click on a picture to enlarge.
See more underwater pictures on our facebook page.
Airport information:
Most international flights arrive at Maiquetia airport (Aeropuerto Internacional “Simon Bolívar”), which is located on the coastline, 26 Km outside of the city centre of Caracas. By taxi it takes about 4 to 5 hours to get to Choroní. International flights arrive and depart worldwide. Airport code: CCS.
The nearest airport to Choroní is Valencia (Aeropuerto Internacional “Arturo Michelena”), which is located just outside the city. By taxi it takes about 2½ hours to get to Choroní. International flights to Miami, Aruba, Bonaire, Curacao and Bogotá. Airport code: VLN.
From the airport, you can take a bus to Caracas. Busses leave in front of the domestic terminal, which is right next to the international terminal.
You’ll have to get a bus to bus-terminal “La Bandera” in Caracas, which is an overcrowded place where you need to be extra alert on your personal belongings.
The bus will take you to the bus-terminal in Maracay, from where you can either take a bus or taxi to Choroní. Busses leave from inside the terminal, while taxi’s leave from outside.
From the airport, you can take a taxi either to Caracas, or directly to Choroní. If you decide to take a taxi directly, it is worthwhile to have us make arrangements with the taxi company in Choroní, to have you picked up, as the airport taxis are more expensive. In Maracay, just behind the bus-terminal you can find a taxi stop which is marked “Puerto Colombia”. From here you can get reasonably cheap to Choroní and Puerto Colombia. The taxi will charge per person, and wait until 4 passengers are present.
From the airport, you can go by bus to bus-terminal “Big Low” in Valencia. Get on a bus in front of the airport-terminal, and ask the driver to notify you where to get off the bus, to take another bus to “Big Low”. From “Big Low” busses leave frequently to Maracay (1 hour).
The bus will take you to the bus-terminal in Maracay, from where you can take either a bus or taxi to Choroní. Busses leave from inside the terminal, while taxi’s leave from outside.
From the airport, you can take a taxi either to bus-terminal “Big Low” in Valencia, the bus-terminal in Maracay, or directly to Choroní. If you decide to take a taxi directly, it is worthwhile to have us make arrangements with the taxi company in Choroní, to have you picked up, as airport taxis are more expensive. In Maracay, just behind the bus-terminal you can find a taxi stop which is marked “Puerto Colombia”. From here you can get reasonably cheap to Choroní and Puerto Colombia. The taxi will charge per person, and wait until 4 passengers are present.
