Personal Data Gathering and Protection
Memorimage has adopted all the safety measures and levels for the protection of personal data as demanded by the Spanish Law 15/1999, dated 13 December, for the Protection of Personal Data and the regulations for its application.
The personal data provided by users of www.memorimagefestival.org are subject to automatic treatment and incorporated into a file belonging to Memorimage, which is similarly responsible for this file.
In this website, the gathering of personal date is carried out purely and exclusively via the subscription form for the newsletter of www.memorimagefestival.org.
Anybody who subscribes to our newsletter implies express consent by the user to include his or her personal date in the aforementioned automatic file of www.memorimagefestival.org.
The file is inscribed in the General Registry of the Spanish Agency for Data Protection, which the user may access to check the situation of his or her data.
The user can exercise his or her right of access, modification, cancellation and opposition in accordance with that contained in the Spanish Law 15/1999, dated 13 December, for the Protection of Personal Data and other applicable laws, by sending an e-mail to the address info@Memorimage.com or by postal mail to the registered address of Memorimage: Calle Mallorca, 209, pral. 08036 Barcelona.
The website www.memorimagefestival.org will not sell, cede or in any way transmit any personal data or information of its users to third parties.
During a visit to the website of Memorimage, certain information of this visit will be automatically stored. A «session cookie» is used in this website for purely statistical reasons.
A «cookie» is a small record that a website stores in a web browser programme.
They are used to obtain information about visits to the website, but they do not store any personal data nor can they be related to the user in question.
This type of cookie disappears when the web browser is closed.
Revue is based on archive propaganda newsreels produced in the USSR in the 50’s and 60’s.
The film shows the almost forgotten side of the Soviet times and the way of thinking at that period.
Its main focus is on the earthy life on the collective farms; the stages of industrialisation and modernization are touched upon with imagery that shows the bustle of factories and the wonders of mechanisation.
It explores the life of people all across the vast expanse of the Soviet Motherland, though full of hardship, deprivation and absurd rituals, but at the same time illuminated by the glorious shining of the communist illusion.
Q&A with film director Sergei Loznitsa.
One of the most prominent Spanish sopranos of the 20th century, Victòria dels Àngels performed on some of the world’s most renowned stages: the Bayreuth Festival, La Scala in Milan, Covent Garden and the Metropolitan Opera House. And she was always surrounded by the most influential and celebrated artists.
Brava, Victòria! reveals the sensitive personality of this singer, who came from a humble household.
Original language: Catalan, Spanish, English
Memorimage and the university students
The Tarragona Group was founded in 1970 by a number of contemporary art artists who followed the trends of informalism, abstract expressionism and the sources of pop.
All of these artists represented a shift in the evolution of the local visual arts scene.
Original language: Catalan
During the three days that the Catalan Republic was in force in 1931, Francesc Macià and Lluís Companys not always had the same point of view.
An intimate journey through the life of soprano Victòria dels Àngels, through her home films, her diaries and her personal belongings.
Evita Peron is a myth in Argentina. The illegitimate daughter of a land owner, she died as the country’s first lady.
Screening of fragments of this film and case of study of the direction, production and research process by Manuel Huerga, Toni Soler and Francesc Escribano.
Session in Catalan.
Through the eyes of Francesc Macià and Lluís Companys, the heroes of one of the most important episodes in the history of Catalonia during the 20th century, we relive the events that took place in Barcelona between 14 and 17 April 1931, the three days that the Catalan Republic was in force.
The chance discovery of the file of letters and replies of the most famous advice column in the history of Spanish radio and its subsequent preservation in a network archive belonging to the Catalan government has enabled the making of a documentary that is unique in its genre. Here, the sole and exclusive star of the film is the original text of the letters written by thousands of women, seeking advice, and the replies that were written by the programme’s editorial team.
Case of study presented by the film director, Josep Rovira, and the archive researcher of the film Montserrat Bailac.
*This film is part of the Section Memories. More information.
The making of... 50 años de tradiciones
Dreamland is a film about the exploitation of natural resources in Iceland and demonstrates that clean energy does not come without consequence.
Iceland is a country blessed with an abundance of clean, renewable, hydro-electric and geothermal energy.
Because Iceland produces more green energy than it needs heavy industry has been moving into the country and companies like Alcoa have been building aluminium smelters.
Clean energy brings in polluting industry.
Dreamland tells the story of a nation with abundance of choices gradually becoming caught up in a plan to turn its beautiful wilderness into a massive system of hydro-electric and geothermal power plants with dams and reservoirs.
The Loss
The well-known German actor Urlich Tukur is the master of ceremonies of this film, which is made up entirely of archival footage.
He takes us on a tour through the inside of the Kabarett scene in Berlin as an eyewitness testimony of the history of the Weimar Republic. Owned by the Jews, the cabarets became the mirror for critical thought on politics and culture, as well as a symbol of Berlin in the 1920’s.
Idioma original: German, French
