The birth in Barcelona of the director’s first nephew, a Cuban that immigrated to Catalonia ten years ago, inspires a journey to the isle that is crossed by a similar one but taken backwards, whom journeyer, Francisco Carulla, visited Catalonia back in 1927 whilst filming with a 16mm camera.
Through Carulla’s eyes, the director discovers the story of this emigration that began in the 19th century, getting to know the experience of those thousands of emigrants that crossed the Atlantic striving for a new, better life.
This film takes part in a strong reflection on identity, roots and emigration, just as a mirror game.
