If our point of departure is the premise that “everyone has a story to tell”, we will appreciate the opportunity to reserve a special space for the most delicate and intimate films that tell the most personal stories.
Most of these tales would not make any sense without their general historical backgrounds. At the same time, they are recounted from the perspective of micro-history.
Stories that shape the Small History.
