Garbo, the Man Who Saved the World is the story of double agent Joan Pujol, a piece of history with almost no existing graphic material. Hence, to offer a first-hand account of this story, the filmmakers drew on a wide range of formats, some existing footage, and particularly archival material from B movies, Hollywood films, newsreels and 3D graphics, which were all combined with an aesthetic style very typical of the time.
Fragments of the documentary will be shown during this session, in which the producer, director and scriptwriter, Edmon Roch, will explain the main aspects of the research and production process.
