Colombia, France and United Kingdom 2010 97 min.
In 2002, Colombia’s presidential candidate, Ingrid Betancourt, was kidnapped by the FARC, along with her campaign manager Clara Rojas. This is the 6-year story of captivity, betrayal, love, hate, attempted escapes, relationships with the kidnappers and her dramatic rescue.
Following her release, nothing would ever be the same.
