Echevarrieta became an ally to the German Marine, taking part in their secret plans through the most eminent spies of the time. They build together the best weapon of their time: the E-1 submarine.
The 6-year story of the kidnapping of Ingrid Betancourt: betrayal, attempted escapes, relationships with the kidnappers and her dramatic rescue.
Vital adventure of Jesús Monzón. Leader of the Communist Party in Navarra, he set in motion a guerrilla movement to combat Franco from the Vall d’Aran valley.
The eternal love story between Nicole and Rafel set us in the 1950's Mallorca where they fell in love.
Come along and join Yuri Gagarin in the first journey of the man through the space.
Fifty years later, the European Space Agency makes the same route.
The revealing story of a man who changed the world with his scissors.
The hairstyles of The Beatles, Mia Farrow and the celebrities of the 1970s.
The use of archival footage typically comes hand in hand with stories of the past. Stories that take us back to events that were significant due to their impact on the future of humanity.
Happy, tragic, inevitable and simple ordinary stories that have written the history of humanity.
The fundamental aim of the Memorimage Festival is to accommodate a type of film that is on the rise yet has not yet found its niche in the festival circuit.
A jury of renowned media professionals and archivists will evaluate the quality and skill with which these productions have incorporated archival imagery into narrative discourse.
Award to the best film in the Official Section. An award of 4.000€ donated by the Reus City Council to the film director.
Award to the best production. An award of 3.000€.
