The sixth edition of Memorimage . International Film Festival of Reus closed on 12 November with an increase in turnout of 68% , with a total of 2,472 participants in the different sessions and side events organized during the festival.
Memorimage reached its sixth edition with 22 films on various topics , but usually with a common point , that "speak not so much as the characters events that have caused these events," as highlighted by the festival's artistic director , Anna Marqués.
The jury also made special mention in the Democratic Memorial Award to the film "Els Brigadistes entre Nosaltres''.
This year the festival has established itself in all its sections and activities tripling the number of attendees in MemoriJove and the Professional Conference where there were 81 attendees.
A section devoted to films for the whole family. Enjoy cinema with your family! Come with your children to rediscover films that are cinema classics.
The screening will be the 7th of November at 17:00h in the Teatre Bartrina
To be able to discover who is the veritable thief, Keaton will take part in some extraordinary adventures in which, by magic, he will get inside the films of his heroes.
Nicole is an elderly woman who was born into a traditional bourgeois family in Paris. In the 1950's, she visited Mallorca, where she met a man well-versed in the art of seducing foreign women (a picador) named Rafel and fell madly in love with him. This led her to leave Paris and take up residence in Alcúdia, where the two lived happily and very much in love.
Though he passed on, Nicole still talks to and dances with her love Rafel and with his memory …
Original language: Catalan, Spanish and French
In keeping with the Festival tradition and as a second chance for those who are unable to see the awarded films the first time round, Memorimage will be offering second screenings of the awarded works in a continuous session at Sala Santa Llúcia on Sunday 8th November, starting at 10:00 am.
United Kingdom and Canada 2015 112 min.
In 1971 a small group of Canadian activists initiated their first mission aboard an old fishing boat: to stop the atomic bomb tests that Nixon was undergoing in Alaska. This was the birth of the environmental movement and the creation of the global organization that today is known as Greenpeace.
Can a bunch of journalists and hippie scientists change the world with only the aid of their cameras?
This group of pacifist ecologists use images as “mind bombs”, capable of transforming consciousness, trusting in the power of images and media as tools of social change.
Even so, activism is disorganized.
The true revolutions have never been able to be organized.
Will they be able to agree in the important mission to save the planet?
Original language:English
