Two proximity probes and a special electronic system were developed in order to be able to supervise filters.
A difference signal is processed by the measuring electronics to allow supervision of the process cycle.
Two proximity probes and two electronic systems were developed in order to be able to supervise filters.
The changing levels, seen in the following example, are measured before and after the filter. The probe signal before the filter can be used to control a tilting furnace.
The probe signal after the filter activates the alarm for a filter change.
A special feature of the system is additional cooling performed by compressed air, which can be used as required.
The company Elektro Carli was founded in 1978 in Bergisch Gladbach near Cologne.
The main purpose of the activities was the manufacturing and start-up of complete systems in chemical plants.
This originally included pumps for liquid metals, level meters and flow meters for handling and monitoring of liquid metals up to 800°C.
The developments were tested for a maximum degree of reliability and efficiency in order to meet the high requirements in this field of technology.
Major investments were made in basic research and development to achieve optimum material matching that offered long-term stability for the prevailing high-temperature environment.
As time passed, we increasingly specialized in this area and after formal restructuring in 1989 and renaming as Carli Electro Automation GmbH, we almost exclusively dealt with level measuring devices and electromagnetic pumps for industrial use at up to 800°C. Carli Electro Automation GmbH not only supplies German foundries, but also those throughout the world. In 2007 Carli Electro Automation GmbH was acquired by Precimeter Scientific, Sweden. The profile of the company remains intact and the products remain the same.
Future with modern technology
Based on many years of experience and continuous developments, Carli Precimeter GmbH manufactures high-quality inductive measuring systems (probes) and pumps that are used in the production processes of foundries.
The inductive measuring systems and pumps from Carli Precimeter GmbH offer the following advantages:
• higher stability of the measured values
• higher material and temperature stability
• a low level of maintenance
The company Carli Precimeter GmbH therefore numbers among the most innovative enterprises in this market section.
The electronics of Carli Precimeter GmbH have been developed especially to meet the high standards of our measuring systems.
The MGK 1000 C unit (analog) is an economically priced high-performance system. It can be used with all Carli Precimeter GmbH probes.
The unit is designed for fitting to a standard rail system. It has a LED in the front cover instead of a display and can be configured with an analog output signal.
The function of the MGK 1000 C unit (robot) replaces the electrode on the bionic arm of the robot.
This unit is designed for contactless detection of the melt surface and has 3 adjustable switch points.
The switch points can be configured as follows.
• working level
The MGK 1000C unit is an economically priced high-performance system. It can be used with all Carli Precimeter GmbH probes.
The unit is designed for fitting to a standard rail system. It has an LED array in the front cover instead of a display and 1-5 adjustable switch points are possible.
The MGK 1002 unit was developed to process dual measuring ranges such as:
• two levels are measured one above the other (as in aluminium or magnesium electrolysis)
The equipment is designed for rail mounting and possesses two digital displays.
The unit MG 2001 is an analog all-round electronic device in a normal housing.
A LCD display and 4 trimming devices are located on the front plate to configure the settings 0%, 100% in addition to limit 1 and limit 2.
A LED display and the keys for the configuration input are located in the front plate.
The equipment is suitable for intermediate installation, particularly in switchgear cabinets or wall housings.
This pump system can be extended for higher flow rates.
The pump is not self extracting.
Therefore at least 1/3 of the pump channel must be filled with molten metal.
The round pump was conceived for the employment at high temperatures to maximally 800°C temperature. The performance of the pump is temperature-dependent.
In order to be able to ensure the performance of the pump, we recommend to keep the magnet frame temperature under 400°C. If necessary a forced air cooling must be used.
In order to obtain an even distribution of alloys in the basic material, Carli Precimeter GmbH has developed a probe to monitor and correct the consistency of the product prior to completion of the end product.
The advantages are:
• no contact with the melt
• accurate approach of the point of reference
In automatic partial soldering, it is necessary that a column of tin with a constant flow is formed.
In order to perform this, Carli Precimeter GmbH has specially developed an electromagnetic pump for this purpose.
The electromagnetic round pump R6-D85 is used for automatic soldering units, e.g. for a partial soldering unit. The advantage is based on a laminar flow by the electromagnetic force and a stable soldering column, free from pulsating effects.
In order to monitor the charging of the furnace, Carli Precimeter GmbH has developed probes that facilitate and guarantee charging of the furnace.
In order to be able to monitor filters or channels in closed or open systems, Carli Precimeter GmbH offers proximity probes that are used to control a tilting furnace or automatic plug unit via electronic output signals.
As an alternative to electrode scanning, Carli Precimeter GmbH offers a purpose-built proximity probe to allow positioning of the exact operating point of the ladle.
• no contact with the melt
• accurate approach of the point of reference
In order to achieve an even distribution of alloys in the basic material, Carli Precimeter GmbH has developed a probe to monitor and correct the consistency of the product prior to completion of the end product.
In order to ensure a continuous, even casting process, Carli Precimeter GmbH has developed a tilting furnace control system consisting of a contactless measuring probe and electronic measurement system.
The analog output signal of the electronic system is connected to the control of the tilting furnace.
Measurement in the high-temperature range
The high-temperature proximity switch is made of stainless material and is therefore designed to suit the rough environment in the companies for which it was made.
Measurement of different levels
Since it is well known that very aggressive chemical reactions take place during electrolysis processes, it is essential to select an appropriate protective tube for the submerged probe.
In order to control the process of low pressure pouring, Carli Precimeter GmbH has developed a ring probe, allowing the casting process to be started from a pre-programmed reference point.
In order to control or influence the level in the channel in closed or open systems, Carli Precimeter GmbH offers proximity probes that use the output signal of the probe electronics, i.o. they help to control the level by accurate positioning of a tilting furnace.
Filling can be performed by a tilting furnace or a plug control unit.
In order to achieve a continuous, low-turbulence casting process in a vertical or horizontal continuous casting plant, Carli Precimeter GmbH has developed an electromotor-driven plug control system.
The system is based on the old scale principle.
The center balance support is adjustable to allow variable speed or force for the specific casting processes.
The plug positioning control consists of a probe to measure the filling level, a drive unit and a control unit.
The measuring systems from Carli Precimeter GmbH are ideally suited to allow continuous control and accurate measurement of the quality of the melt during the process, consisting of one or more proximity probes and the control unit or drive unit.
Two chamber system
Various different measuring systems from Carli Precimeter GmbH can be employed for the optimum monitoring and control of a two chamber system.
An economically priced compact system is the Model MGK 1002, which offers the advantage of being able to process both probe systems simultaneously.
Based on the belief that our customers acquire a high-quality standard in purchasing our products, they deserve the best service available.
Consequently, Carli Precimeter GmbH offers the following services to its customers:
• Support during integration of products in existingsystems
and processes
• Co-operation in the development of customised solutions
• Co-operation with institutes and universities
• Start-up, briefings and training courses
This pump system can be extended modular for higher performance The pump is not self extracting, this only works if at least 1/3 of the pump system is filled with the liquid medium.
The flat channel pump was conceived for the employment at high temperatures to maximally 800°C temperature.
The performance of the pump is temperature-dependent.
Complete systems from Carli Precimeter GmbH offer the advantage of the ability of implementing complex processes in a closed-circuit system.
Working procedures in casting plants require and optimum in terms of precision and reliability.
Carli Precimeter GmbH offers products that assist in optimally monitoring and controlling casting processes in casting plants. Please press here for the Precimeter Group homepage: www.precimeter.com
The specimen application shows the arrangement of a vertical continuous casting process using our measuring system.
The specimen application shows the arrangement of a vertical continuous casting process using our measuring system to obtain a continuous casting process, in spite of a long channel and an uneven metal surface. In addition, the entire channel system is monitored by double probe detection to prevent overflow.
The specimen application shows the arrangement of a vertical continuous casting process, which operates with two systems from Carli Precimeter GmbH.
Example of use, showing a casting process in which our measuring system performs two tasks:
• Controlling the tilting furnace by means of a proximity probe, in order to
maintain a constant level in the channel.
The output signal of 0-20 mA or 0-10 V can be used to control the tilting furnace.
The system is based on a balance principle, in which the centre point of the balance can be variably adjusted to allow adaptation to different speeds in the casting process.
The plug control consists of a probe to sense the level, a drive and a control unit.
Emptying of containers with liquid molten mass is always a risky process, involving dangers.
In this connection, CARLI ELECTRO AUTOMATION GMBH has developed a pump system with a round pump that makes the process controllable and safe.
For stationary, non-tilting melting furnaces, there is often the need to cover large distances in order to tap the molten mass in conjunction with considerable mechanical effort, which under certain circumstances influences the statistics of the furnace and the building.
In order to automate removal of the molten mass, Carli Precimeter GmbH has developed a system based on an electromagnetic pump (flat channel pump).
Other materials on request!
Inductive level measuring systems are used to regulate, control or measure filling levels in melt and holding furnaces, intermediate vessels, channels and launders.
The measuring systems are available in a submersible version and a non-contact version.
The submersible probes from Carli Precimeter GmbH are a high-tech product. They work in the immersed condition with an appropriate protective tube at a melt temperature of up to 800°C and can therefore also be used in closed systems without forced air cooling.
With an airtight adapter available from Carli Precimeter GmbH, the probes can also be used in closed systems with low pressure castings.
Only the best quality materials are used, combined with a good quality assurance system. Each probe is tested before delivery and the results are documented.
The "continuous immersion probe" is a system that directly registers the exact level in the melt through a protective tube.
Standard lengths are up to a meter. Further lengths are possible.
The continuous (dual) level probe was developed in order to be able to measure two superimposed levels (e.g. magnesium/salt, aluminium/salt).
This application is typical in the electrolysis of primary metal.
This submersible probe version also needs an appropriate protective tube.
The homogeneity submerged probe is intended to assist casters in achieving good homogeneity after fusion of the base material with alloy additives as the final product without major differences in the concentration of alloyed material.
The probes work in the immersed condition at a temperature of up to 800°C and can be used in closed systems without forced air cooling.
A gastight adapter is required for the appropriate sealing.
The measuring range depends on the diameter of the probe. For the standard probe with a probe diameter of 115 mm, a measuring range of 100 mm is achieved.
A major advantage is remote operation in relation to the melt.
The probe should not come into direct contact with liquid metal.
For extreme applications in which heavy splashing cannot be ruled out, the probe should be protected with a monalite protection hood.
The probes can withstand up to 800°C and can also be used in closed systems without forced air cooling.
They must not however come into contact with an open fire, e.g. burners, since the operating temperature of the probe can easily be exceeded as a result.
The light version of the ring probe was developed to measure the melt inside a ceramic riser tube in low-pressure casting systems.
The ring probe is pushed over the tubing, so that the injection process can be started with rising melt from a preadjusted reference point.
The heavy version of the ring probe replaces the connection between the holding furnace and mould (upper tool part) for low pressure pouring.
During the casting process, the melt rises in a tube into the ring probe area.
The casting process can be started from a preadjusted reference point.
Advantages:
• no contact with the melt
• exact reference starting point
Charging monitoring and level measurement with wider fluctuations in level
With open furnace systems the proximity probe and the appropriate electronics can be used with up to 5 switching points to accurately indicate and monitor the filling level.
A proximity probe is used when the accuracy of the dosages depends on small bath fluctuations.
Charging system
A submerged probe is used in the fusion chamber for greater fluctuations in the charging.
To influence the process of low pressure pouring, a ring probe was designed by Carli Precimeter GmbH. The Ring probe is positioned over the riser tube, so that during an increase in pressure the rising melt reaches the area of the ring probe at a pre-programmed point of reference.
This point is used for the start of the casting process.
