If you wish to travel in time and music, this year you should spend your new year’s eve in Cagliari!
The journey goes from 1943 to 2013. In some of the most beautiful piazzas of the historical centre, will be possible to listen and to bring back different kind of music and atmospheres, decade by decade, of these last seventy years.
1943, for the town, is a terrible time during the war, when the bombs almost destroyed the whole centre, but it also marks a new beggning, a rebirth for Cagliari.
The idea is to make the piazzas and the town in a suggestive place where to meet, listen to music and dance all together, living the centre as a unique outdoor stage, where people and music are the main actors.
The whole experience attempts to immerse you in a spellbinding outdoor set design, with vintage images projections, dreamy lights, retro atmospheres and architectural lighting, to celebrate the arrival of the new year and the town itself.
The beginning of the party is set for 09,30 p.m., for each location, the last day of this almost gone year!
So, do not miss this unique chance to travel in time, and music in the very beautiful town of Cagliari! Waiting for you, happy New Year!
Architecture and museums
Sardinia in Salsa is one of the major festivals dedicated to the salsa in the world, which has been taking place annually for 3 years in Sardinia.
It is a week entirely dedicated to the salsa, with the presence of the main international masters, who will give classes, seminars and other lessons as well as amazing performances to entertain fans and audience.
Host of this event dedicated to Caribbean dancing?
The Flamingo Resort is a beach resort that offers luxury suites as well as an amazing spa center to its guests.
The manifestation consists of more than 45 seminars and workshops dedicated to Latin dance, given by a selection of the best salsa teachers of Europe. Each night, very different parties will be organized to entertain students and fans.
The Poco Loco in Alghero, in cooperation with Centro Commerciale Naturale Alghero in Centro and the city of Alghero, from 13 to 27 April hosts the 2012 edition of April Jazz Festival.
The international Jazz meets in Alghero, a melting pot of various jazz cultures starring international, sardinian and national artists for an unmissable set of concerts.
Each performance will be characterised by a different theme in a combination of jazz, smooth, funk, rock and more.
A varied program that will please everyone, even those new to jazz.
Its the second year in a row Cagliari celebrate the pride, but the very first one for the entire region.
The Sardinia Pride will also conclude a number of appointments such as meetings, seminars, debates and exhibition, happening during the forty days before the date of the pride, calling the whole: Queeresima FACEBOOK QUEERESIMA CAGLIARI
