Very proud of its past, Sassari was the last capital city of the Sardinian Giudicati and in 1294 it became a Free Municipality confederated to Genoa.
In 1417 it became a royal city during the Aragonese reign. Besides the monuments that testify its long history, Sassari is well-known for its cuisine (which is very rich and characterized by peerless flavours) and for its closeness to Platamona beach (known as the beach of people from Sassari) and that of Stintino, one of the whitest and most beautiful in the Mediterranean Sea.
Sassari is 12km from the port of Porto Torres and 35km from the airport of Alghero-Fertilia.
All its rooms are comfortable and equipped with private bathroom with hair-dryer, minibar, satellite TV, direct telephone.
In the restaurant hall of this hotel the guests can taste the local and national cuisine.
