The villa is in the area of Villasimius, locality of Is Traias, near Simius, perhaps the most renowned in the territory of Villasimius.
The type of construction dates back to the early eighties and are mostly spread over the hill that ends on the beach. It is a beautiful bay protected from the wind, about 150 meters long and at least 25 meters wide with the usual semicircle shape.
To one side of the bay two beautiful reefs enclose the white sandy beach. It does not have beach establishment and the access is free and by car up to a distance of one hundred metres.
Full of typical Mediterranean vegetation, low and shaped by the wind. Location
It is possible to access the villa from the road through a stairway to the garden (where there is the outside shower) and the spacious equipped veranda in front of the villa; it has a wide granit table; from here it is possible to access the lounge where there are two sofas, TV, the kitchenette with oven and fridge.
Three steps down lead to the first bathroom and the three rooms (semi basement floor since the villa is located on a slope); these three rooms: one double and the others with bunk beds (one of which has a third bed) have very little space and basement windows that allow not only enough ventilation but also fresh air during the hottest period.
A flight of stairs leads to the mezzanine floor where there is another bedroom equipped with air conditioning and another full bathroom.
This room has a door that leads to the veranda in the back of the house, where there is a barbecue, a washing machine and another granite table, this veranda is accessible via a few steps from the parking as well where it is possible to safely park up to three cars. Last and very important note: this house has water reservoir.
water basin
