The Albergo Diffuso Mannois (country hotel) offers an innovative type of hospitality based on the reception of tourists in real town places and the revaluation of both the territory and the historic town centre.
The hotel is composed by 3 buildings: Sa Corte (main building): a typical rustic house with rural architecture of the nineteenth century, inhabited by 3 ancient families of farmers.
Guests who will stay here will be catapulted into the past and in the history of our ancestors.
Seven rooms, the bar, the reception and the breakfast room are located in this building. Sa Dommo: a typical house in the town centre of Orosei with large areas, verandas, elegant and bright spaces with a view on the Tuttavista Mount; five rooms are located in this area.
Sa Turre a fascinating building, which has also been the first guesthouse in Orosei during the Seventies.
In this building are located 6 rooms, about 150 metres from Sa Dommo.
Guests staying in Sa Turre will enjoy an extraordinary view overlooking the Gulf of Orosei.
The Albergo Diffuso Mannois is in Orosei, 800 metres from the sea and some of the most beautiful beaches of Sardinia. Beach available to guests in Marina di Orosei.
The Albergo Diffuso Mannois has 18 rooms distributed in the 3 buildings.
All the accommodation are situated in the old town, close together and united by the reception services.
All the rooms are different, each recalling its past, and have a separate entrance.
Two rooms are designed to ensure maximum comfort to disabled guests.
Breakfast is served in the breakfast room located in the main building. During the summer, breakfast is served in the courtyard, where is also possible to have a drink.
