In this page you will find all the answers to the most frequently asked questions. This is because we want to clarify all the details about Atlantidea Viaggi travel agency, the web portal and about the reservations.
1. How can I book a holiday package to Sardinia or a hotel, residence, villa or holiday house, a Farm Tourism or a B&B?
Booking your holiday is very easy.
You must only go through and choose the payment method you prefer: by credit card (Visa or Mastercard), by bank money transfer or by postal order.
You will be sent a confirmation of your holiday that you will be asked to pay entirely or with a 30 % deposit.
In the first case you will be immediately sent the voucher and the invoice.
Or, in the second case, the travel documents will be sent after acquittance of the total amount., by 30 days before arrival date.
And even more. We can also offer to you an insurance for medical assistance with Europe Assistance company.
2. What kind of payment methods do you accept for booking an accommodation or a holiday package and what are the extra charges for each payment method (bank transfer or credit card commissions)?
- By credit card Visa or Mastercard, with verified secure system by Visa and MasterCard, without charges if you buy straight on the internet through our portal.
- With PayPal, a secure system, by credit card Visa, Mastecard or PostePay.
In this case as well if you buy straight on the internet though our portal, you will not be charged any extra commissions, on the contrary in case you send a request to our booking center then you will be charged a commission of 1.5% on the total amount..
- With postal order, to the following address: Portale Sardegna srl, Via San Benedetto, 88 - 09129 - Cagliari 3. Why do I have to make a full payment before arrival?
A 30% deposit on the total amount is mandatory for ensuring your accommodation is definitely booked.
Credit Cards are not accepted as security for your holiday.
4. I have got a pet, where is she/he welcome?
5. What are the rules I have to abide to as customer and you have to abide to as supplier of tourist service?
Visit the dedicated page click here.
6. Can you help me choosing the most suitable place to spend a holiday in Sardinia?
Without a thorough knowledge of the territory is very easy to mistake.
Click here : you get a selection of the most beautiful beaches in Sardinia and directions on how to reach them.
8. What are the flights and ferries to Sardinia and how do transports work from/to Sardinia?
In the section dedicated to transports in our website Sardegne.com you will find all information on transports from/to Sardinia and all the information on how to move around.
9. What can I visit in Sardinia apart from the beaches or seaside towns and cities?
There are thousands of things to do and see away from the beaches and summer tourism.
Our mission is to make the tourists aware that two « Sardinian » exist : seaside sardinia and far-away-from-the-sea Sardinia that is to say the one of culture, archeology and history, of food&wine traditions, of cultural heritage, of the cities, of the inner areas, of the nuraghes and mines. Enter the section and you will find several information to undertake your journey into our enchanting island.
10. In case of trouble at the arrival in Sardinia, who can I turn to?
When you buy a holiday through Sardegne.com you do not have to worry: once arrived you wont be left alone.
Our operators will be at your disposal for any further need or problem, a change in the dates or whatever concerns your health. We wish nothing bad ever happens but just in case, be aware that our professionals are ready to help you.
11. Prices and tariffs I can see on sardegne.com are the lowest in the market? And the prices are those given or do I have to pay for any agency fees?
The prices you can find on Sardegne.com are the same as those of the accommodating facilities in Sardinia So you will never find lower prices than those on our website.
12. Can I have the descriptions of the accommodating facilities in a printable format?
13. Do I have to pay any entrance fees at the arrival?
The Regional Council has approved a law concerning taxation on secondary houses, planes and entrance fee which from June to September 2008 will be enforced to non resident people on holiday for 1 € per day.
The same tax will be included in the facility's total cost but will appear in the invoice.
14. What are the roads like in Sardinia? Is it easy to move around?
Roads in Sardinia are not very comfortable.
