Big and small islands, big and small inlets, suggestive ravines, white and pink sandy beaches, wind that blows on the rocks and the sea: this is the Archepelago La Maddalena.
The area, between Bonifacio and the Emerald Coast, covered with Mediterranean vegetation, has an important natural, historical and cultural value (Napoleon, Nelson and Garibaldi left their mark).
The complex, located very near the sea, has been recently build and it has four levels.
La Maddalena is the biggest island of the homonymous archipelago, at 10 minutes boat from Palau, in the northest part of Sardinia.
The hotel is at approx 800 meters from the centre.
There are also wider Junior Suites available and special rooms for handicapped people.
The Hotel has a restaurant with panoramic view.
A particular attention is given to typical Sardinian dishes.
